WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.787
Gate 9 keeps it all true, and
without it everything slowly decays.

2
00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:07.612
It starts with the pilot,
not after cut-over.

3
00:00:07.612 --> 00:00:13.062
First, the CISO decides severity
and response times, decision D-A8.

4
00:00:13.062 --> 00:00:15.649
Then two comparisons run on a schedule.

5
00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:19.428
On the left, HR against the
directory: missing identities,

6
00:00:19.428 --> 00:00:24.009
stale access for people who've left,
orphan accounts, attribute drift,

7
00:00:24.009 --> 00:00:27.787
unauthorized writes, credential
drift and schema drift.

8
00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:31.900
The severities are the program's
defaults, not an external standard.

9
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.597
On the right, the unit and role registry
against the tenant: unit rules that

10
00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:38.369
drifted, paused processing,

11
00:00:38.369 --> 00:00:42.450
role assignments nobody approved,
and restriction mismatches.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.350
Each track's own reconciliation
feeds the same findings queue.

13
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.138
Expect a burst of high-severity
findings in the first month.

14
00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:53.760
That's the measurement finally
working, not the pipeline failing.
